  {
    "episode_id": 49034,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/9/49034.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 3,
    "turn_text": "UFOs have been a hot topic in the federal space over the last couple of years since the Defense Department confirmed the authenticity of videos depicting military pilot sightings of unexplainable phenomena and formed the unidentified aerial phenomena task force. Years before that, there was a much quieter program under the Pentagon's purview, which I just mentioned earlier, the AATIP, that conducted very relevant work. The program was unclassified, but unpublicized, and it was largely funded at your request from Congress, Senator Reid. More than 20 million was secured to back it. To kick off this chat, why don't you tell us a little bit more about what really sparked your inspiration and motivation to advocate for investments in this realm and to really push the Pentagon to prioritize UFO investigations?",
