  {
    "episode_id": 49034,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/9/49034.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 6,
    "turn_text": "And what we did, we put it out to bid. And we wanted to, I wanted to find out how many people had seen these unusual sightings. And it, as it turned out, it wasn't dozens, it wasn't hundreds, thousands of people. We have counts going for 70 years of people seeing these phenomenon. Now, it's becoming even more apparent that these unidentified flight phenomenon exists. What they are, we don't know. The more we study, the less we know what they are. But what we do know is things are developing. For example, in the USSO law, the cruiser and the same ocean, the coast of San Diego, They saw a big object shaped like a football. It was as big as a football field. And it comes and hovers around the cruiser, which is a big, big ship. And then suddenly it just goes into the water and disappears. And there were people saw this with their eyes. And for the first time through radar, sonar, and other new equipment, we have pictures that are scientifically saved. So I'm glad we're looking into this. It's something that I want the, what I want more than anything else to make sure the government doesn't try to hide anything. It must be transparent. Whatever they learn, American people are entitled to know. American people can, whatever the results are, we can handle it. Someone asked me, what if they show us coming someplace else? So what? They asked the same question at President Obama, and he said, look, we're just at a small speck in this great universe. And I wouldn't be surprised if there's something else from someplace else. So that's where we are. I'm glad I got it started. But it's not getting in by the fact that we got something started. Something must be ongoing and transparent to the American people.",
